IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei7-related-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23): RELATED PROVISIONS of 2012 to 2015 other than 2012, c. 19, ss. 251 to 270
-- (those are in ei7-related-2012-tribunal): 2012, c. 19, s. 616; 2012, c. 27, ss. 32 and 33; 2013, c. 35, s. 4;
-- 2014, c. 20, s. 250; 2015, c. 36, s. 79 (src:3763-3793). 2012, c. 31, s. 456 (src:3777-3779) has no rule: it is `inert`.
-- Written by piece ei7 (Sonnet 5.5). Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
-- Seat: the person who has lost work or cannot work, asking which version of a section governs their claim.
-- The amendments are not here; a rule below says whether the amendment reaches the person's claim, benefit period
-- or week. A day that an amending Act fixes by "the day on which ... come into force" is not in the deposited
-- texts, so it is a DATE input.

§ `2012, c. 19, s. 616 - section 14 as amended`

-- src:3763 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 616
-- src:3764 | Transitional
-- src:3765 | 616 Section 14 of the Employment Insurance Act, as amended by section 604, applies only to claimants whose benefit period is established on or after April 7, 2013.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 616 (src:3765)
`Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 616 April 7, 2013` MEANS YearMonthDay 2013 4 7

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 616 (src:3765)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period is established` IS A DATE  -- out of range: sections 9 and 10, when a benefit period is established (piece ei1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 616 section 14 as amended by section 604 applies to the claimant` IF
    `the day on which the benefit period is established` AT LEAST `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 616 April 7, 2013`

§ `2012, c. 27, ss. 32 and 33`

-- s. 32: the amended sections 18, 21 and 152.03 apply "only to claims for benefits because of illness, injury or
-- quarantine that are made for weeks that begin on or after the day" sections 15, 16 and 21 come into force.
-- The reason is the core's `Reason for benefits`.
-- src:3767 | — 2012, c. 27, s. 32
-- src:3768 | Illness, injury or quarantine
-- src:3769 | 32 Sections 18, 21 and 152.03 of the Employment Insurance Act, as amended by sections 15, 16 and 21, apply only to claims for benefits because of illness, injury or quarantine that are made for weeks that begin on or after the day on which sections 15, 16 and 21 come into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 27, s. 32 (src:3769)
GIVEN `the reason for the benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits`  -- out of range: section 12(3) (piece ei1); section 152.14(1) (piece ei5); the core's Reason for benefits
      `the first day of the week for which the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which sections 15, 16 and 21 of the 2012 Act come into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 27 s. 32 sections 18, 21 and 152.03 as amended apply to the claim` IF
        `the reason for the benefits` EQUALS `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`
    AND `the first day of the week for which the claim is made` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 15, 16 and 21 of the 2012 Act come into force`

-- s. 33: sections 23.2 and 152.061 apply to a claimant for any benefit period (a) that begins on or after the day;
-- or (b) that has not ended before that day, but only for weeks of benefits that begin on or after that day.
-- src:3771 | — 2012, c. 27, s. 33
-- src:3772 | Child’s critical illness
-- src:3773 | 33 Sections 23.2 and 152.061 of the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by sections 18 and 23, apply to a claimant for any benefit period
-- src:3774 | (a) that begins on or after the day on which sections 18 and 23 come into force; or
-- src:3775 | (b) that has not ended before that day, but only for weeks of benefits that begin on or after that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 27, s. 33 (src:3773-3775)
GIVEN `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 9 and 10, benefit period (piece ei1); sections 152.1 and 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the first day of the week of benefits` IS A DATE
      `the day on which sections 18 and 23 of the 2012 Act come into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 27 s. 33 sections 23.2 and 152.061 apply to the week of benefits` IF
        `the benefit period`'s `first day of the period` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 18 and 23 of the 2012 Act come into force`
    OR  (    `the benefit period`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 18 and 23 of the 2012 Act come into force`
         AND `the first day of the week of benefits` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 18 and 23 of the 2012 Act come into force`)

§ `2013, c. 35, s. 4 - weeks of confinement in a jail`

-- The new paragraphs 10(10)(a) and 152.11(11)(a) "do not apply ... in respect of any week for which the claimant or the
-- self-employed person was confined ... before the coming into force of this Act". A week is identified by its Sunday
-- (the keel's convention). Fork F7: the text does not say what happens to a week that began before the day and
-- ended on or after it; the week must end before the day, so such a week falls under the new paragraphs.
-- src:3781 | — 2013, c. 35, s. 4
-- src:3782 | Transitional
-- src:3783 | 4 Paragraphs 10(10)(a) and 152.11(11)(a) of the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by sections 2 and 3, respectively, do not apply to the benefit period of a claimant or a self-employed person, as the case may be, in respect of any week for which the claimant or the self-employed person was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution before the coming into force of this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2013, c. 35, s. 4 (src:3783)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
      `the claimant or the self-employed person was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the 2013 Act comes into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2013 c. 35 s. 4 paragraphs 10(10)(a) and 152.11(11)(a) do not apply to the week` IF
        `the claimant or the self-employed person was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution for the week`
    AND `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` `the first day of the week` LESS THAN `the day on which the 2013 Act comes into force`

§ `2014, c. 20, s. 250 - subsections 18(2) and 152.03(1.1)`

-- src:3785 | — 2014, c. 20, s. 250
-- src:3786 | Illness, injury or quarantine
-- src:3787 | 250 Subsections 18(2) and 152.03(1.1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by sections 247 and 248, apply only to claims for benefits because of illness, injury or quarantine that are made for weeks that begin on or after the day on which sections 247 and 248 come into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2014, c. 20, s. 250 (src:3787)
GIVEN `the reason for the benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits`  -- out of range: section 12(3) (piece ei1); section 152.14(1) (piece ei5); the core's Reason for benefits
      `the first day of the week for which the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which sections 247 and 248 of the 2014 Act come into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2014 c. 20 s. 250 subsections 18(2) and 152.03(1.1) as enacted apply to the claim` IF
        `the reason for the benefits` EQUALS `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`
    AND `the first day of the week for which the claim is made` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 247 and 248 of the 2014 Act come into force`

§ `2015, c. 36, s. 79 - compassionate care benefits`

-- A period under 23.1(4) (or 152.06(3)) "as it read immediately before January 3, 2016" that has begun before that day
-- but has not ended: sections 12 and 23.1 (152.06 and 152.14) as they read on that day apply from that day. "Has not
-- ended" is read as: the last day of the period is that day or later.
-- src:3789 | — 2015, c. 36, s. 79
-- src:3790 | Compassionate care benefits
-- src:3791 | 79 (1) If a period referred to in subsection 23.1(4) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before January 3, 2016, has begun in respect of a claimant — as defined in subsection 2(1) of that Act — before that day but has not ended, then sections 12 and 23.1 of that Act, as they read on that day, apply to that claimant beginning on that day.
-- src:3792 | Compassionate care benefits — self-employed persons
-- src:3793 | (2) If a period referred to in subsection 152.06(3) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before January 3, 2016, has begun in respect of a self-employed person — as defined in subsection 152.01(1) of that Act — before that day but has not ended, then sections 152.06 and 152.14 of that Act, as they read on that day, apply to that person beginning on that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2015, c. 36, s. 79 (src:3791)
`Act RP 2015 c. 36 s. 79 January 3, 2016` MEANS YearMonthDay 2016 1 3

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2015, c. 36, s. 79(1) (src:3791)
GIVEN `the period referred to in subsection 23.1(4), as it read immediately before January 3, 2016` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 23.1(4), the compassionate care period (piece ei1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2015 c. 36 s. 79(1) sections 12 and 23.1 as they read on January 3, 2016 apply to the claimant from that day` IF
        `the period referred to in subsection 23.1(4), as it read immediately before January 3, 2016`'s `first day of the period` LESS THAN `Act RP 2015 c. 36 s. 79 January 3, 2016`
    AND `the period referred to in subsection 23.1(4), as it read immediately before January 3, 2016`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST `Act RP 2015 c. 36 s. 79 January 3, 2016`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2015, c. 36, s. 79(2) (src:3793)
GIVEN `the period referred to in subsection 152.06(3), as it read immediately before January 3, 2016` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 152.06(3), the compassionate care period (piece ei5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2015 c. 36 s. 79(2) sections 152.06 and 152.14 as they read on January 3, 2016 apply to the self-employed person from that day` IF
        `the period referred to in subsection 152.06(3), as it read immediately before January 3, 2016`'s `first day of the period` LESS THAN `Act RP 2015 c. 36 s. 79 January 3, 2016`
    AND `the period referred to in subsection 152.06(3), as it read immediately before January 3, 2016`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST `Act RP 2015 c. 36 s. 79 January 3, 2016`
